  "notes": "BAKED STANDALONE (2026-07-25): this was a frame_alias of wh3_dlc_ie_parchment_map_english.jpg, which was removed from sources/. Because the alias affine was measured exactly, the parent's fitted control points transfer through it without loss, so the placement is unchanged - only the indirection is gone. Re-deriving now means re-fitting this record directly rather than correcting a parent. Annotated twin of the IE parchment master: each macro region outlined in a saturated hue and labelled with its Immortal Empires province count. Consumed by worldgen/macro.py, which recovers the contours by DIFFERENCING this against the clean master rather than by thresholding it - a difference cancels the coats of arms and other artwork present in both, which no colour rule survives. Contributes macro grouping only: boundary/coastline/relief precedence 0, because its added strokes would read as spurious province borders. The printed counts (Empire 22, Cathay 19, Lustria 21, ...) are carried in macro.PRINTED_COUNTS as a sanity check on the grouping, never as a target for our own state count.",
